    "media:imagetext": "20°N\n20°W\n20°\n40°E\n60° E\n80°E\nPAN-AMERICAN AIRWAYS AFRICA LTD\nathurstc\n460\nFrench West Africă\nLake\nRoberts Field\nLiberia\nGold Coast\n1-- Feb-Dec 42\nКолод\nEquator\nTakoradiO °O24\u003e\nMain Trans-Africa\nRouter\n327 Feb-Dec 42\n230ct 41-12 Dec 42\n14 Nov 41-\nMardiguni\nFrench Equatorial Africa:\nA°\n1941-1942\n\" Pioneering\n\"Hump\nApril-May 1942\n25\nAug-Nov 42 Lydda\nChina\nCAIRO\nДеся\nPalestine\nHabbaniya\nDelivery Plans\nChungking\n653\nEgypt\n0252\nO\nand Cargo to Russia\nTeheran 1\n(also 36 Pan Africa\nBasra O\n1 June - 19 Octy42\nDinjaniew)\nMyitkyina\nJan-Dec 42\nIran\nNew Delhi\ncooch\nO\n-Kunming\nAnglo\nEgyptian\nLuxor\n58g\n631\nBehar\n8. Sudan\nSharjah O\n735\nApr\n•Eritrea\nKarachig\n785\nO\nLashio\n4420 Asmaras\nCalcutta\nGeneina\nMasirah Island\n523 KHARTOUMO Aden Aug-Nov 42\n62*\nBurma\nEvacuation\n86 Dec 41-Decí42\nFeb-Dec\nSalalah 6 June-1 Aug 42\nJune- Aug 42\nApril-May 1942\nTrans-Atlantic\nFerry Route\n(from Natal, Brazil)\n• Ascension Island\nThe dates shown (in blue) are the periods of\nPan-Africa's deployment at each station.\nHowever, the larger figures showing staff\nnumbers are those on\n1 September 1942\nwhen the total employee count was 1,016.\nBlack figures show airway distances (statute\nmiles. Total, Bathurst-Karachi 7371 via Cairo,\n6422 via Aden.\nEquator\nAFRICA\n.:.\n40°E\n60°E\n80° E\nREGD",
